cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Itinera, please cite this software. Itinera is a from-scratch
  reimplementation of the core ideas of the R package leastcostpath (Joseph
  Lewis); please also cite that upstream work where appropriate.
title: "Itinera – Least-Cost Pathways: anisotropic movement modelling for archaeology"
abstract: >-
  Itinera is a QGIS plugin for anisotropic movement modelling in archaeology:
  least-cost paths (LCP), least-cost corridors (LCC), From-Everywhere-To-
  Everywhere (FETE), Randomized Shortest Paths, circuit-theory connectivity,
  multi-criteria cost surfaces, accessibility / cost catchments, sensitivity
  analysis, and route validation (Path Deviation Index + buffer overlap). It
  implements ten cost functions (Tobler on/off-path, Herzog, Naismith, Llobera
  & Sluckin, Irmischer & Clarke, Minetti, load-aware Pandolf, and wheeled /
  pack-animal critical-slope presets) plus an interactive map-click tool for
  point-to-point LCP. Built on the numpy/scipy geostack bundled with QGIS, it
  requires no external pip dependencies. The pure-numerics core is also
  published as the `itinera` PyPI library. Itinera is a from-scratch
  reimplementation of the core ideas of the R package leastcostpath
  (Joseph Lewis).
